{"reference":"1 Chronicles 26","book":"1 Chronicles","chapter":26,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Reading the Orders","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The detailed Levitical and administrative orders in this part of 1 Chronicles may preserve earlier traditions, but they may also reflect and authorize later temple institutions. For that reason, it is historically disputed whether the arrangements in chapter 26 should be projected directly onto a single moment in David’s reign.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_chronicles_026_c666f8cdc4893186d7ad9451"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}